<!-- PROOF -->
<section class="lp-proof" id="provenance">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-reveal" style="text-align:center">
      <div class="lp-eyebrow">The proof</div>
      <h2 class="lp-h2">Proof that outlives <em>any app.</em></h2>
      <p class="lp-lede" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto" data-claim="f-shared-cert-view f-shared-cert-verify-result a-032-provenance-transfer">Its certificate is signed when it&rsquo;s issued and timestamped on Bitcoin, so anyone can check that the record still matches what was signed and that it existed before a specific block. When the work moves on, the record goes with it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-phones">
      <div class="lp-phone lp-reveal" data-claim="f-shared-cert-view">
        <div class="frame"><img src="assets/landing/app-cert-qr.jpg" alt="An Attesté certificate in the app, with its verification QR code" loading="lazy" width="600" height="1300"></div>
        <h3>A certificate with a QR code</h3>
        <p>Print it, frame it, send it. Whoever scans it opens the live record.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-phone lp-reveal" data-claim="f-shared-cert-verify-result">
        <div class="frame"><img src="assets/landing/app-btc-anchor.jpg" alt="The Bitcoin anchor panel on an Attesté certificate" loading="lazy" width="600" height="1300"></div>
        <h3>Timestamped on Bitcoin</h3>
        <p>A short fingerprint of the record, never your data. Anyone can check the proof without Attesté.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="lp-phone lp-reveal" data-claim="f-shared-cert-nfc-scan">
        <div class="frame"><img src="assets/landing/app-nfc-verified.jpg" alt="Scanning an NFC tag opens the work's certificate in Attesté" loading="lazy" width="600" height="1300"></div>
        <h3>Tap the frame</h3>
        <p>A small NFC tag on the back of the frame opens the work&rsquo;s certificate on your phone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ASK YOUR AI (claim-gated: tier 0 only) -->
<section class="lp-ai" id="ask-ai" data-claim="f-agent-connector-t0-verify">
  <div class="lp-wrap">
    <div class="lp-ai-card lp-reveal">
      <video muted loop playsinline preload="none" data-ambient poster="assets/landing/ai-chat.jpg" aria-label="An AI assistant checks an Attesté certificate through the public connector"><source src="assets/landing/ai-chat.mp4" type="video/mp4"></video>
    </div>
    <div class="lp-reveal">
      <div class="lp-eyebrow">Connect your AI</div>
      <h2 class="lp-h2">Ask the AI you <em>already use.</em></h2>
      <p class="lp-lede">Attesté runs a public connector that any assistant supporting the Model Context Protocol (MCP) can plug into. Add it once, then paste a certificate link into the chat. Your assistant can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>check whether a certificate&rsquo;s signature holds, and what it records</li>
        <li>fetch the Bitcoin timestamp proof, so anyone can check it without Attesté</li>
        <li>read the work&rsquo;s ownership history, shown as roles and dates, never names</li>
        <li>explain what all of that proves, and what it doesn&rsquo;t</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="lp-url"><code>https://mcp.atteste.art/mcp</code><button type="button" data-copy="https://mcp.atteste.art/mcp">Copy</button></div>
      <p class="lp-small">Read-only. Nothing to sign in to. It can&rsquo;t see your collection, change anything, or buy or sell. <a href="/agents">Full setup guide &rarr;</a></p>
      <p class="lp-small">The chat on the left replays the connector&rsquo;s real answer for a live certificate.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

